## 5. Station representativeness ({{ years }} only)

**Why only {{ years }}.** The following year is replayed hour by hour as if it were production, with a model frozen at the end of {{ rep.design_last_year }} (validation report). No outcome from that year enters this analysis. The gates, on the other hand, check data availability and validity (bounds, duplicates) over the whole window, as a production pipeline would; no value from that year enters this analysis.

**Method.** For each temperature source, each day's mean demand is explained by heating degree-days (how far the day's mean temperature is below {{ rep.base_c|num }} °C), cooling degree-days (above {{ rep.base_c|num }} °C) and the day of the week, by least squares. R² is the share of the variation in daily demand that this model reproduces. All sources are compared on the same {{ rep.days|num }} days ({{ rep.winter_days }} winter days, December to February).

